SUMMARY:Deadline: CISAC (Stanford): Fellowships 2027-2028 (AI\, Nuclear & I
 nternational Security)
DESCRIPTION:CISAC's 2027-2028 fellowship application is open across seven t
 racks: Artificial Intelligence and Laws of Armed Conflict\; AI in Strategi
 c Stability and Military Competition\; Geopolitics of Artificial Intellige
 nce\; India-U.S.\n\nOrganisation: Center for International Security and Co
 operation (CISAC)\, Stanford FSI\nLocation: Stanford\, California\, USA (i
 n-residence\; fellows are expected to be fully present and engaged at CISA
 C)\nAward: Funded in-residence fellowship. Predoctoral fellows receive sti
 pends comparable to the Stanford Graduate Fellowships program\, plus CISAC
  pays non-matriculated student tuition\; postdoctoral and junior-faculty/p
 rofessional fellows receive stipends commensurate with experience and Stan
 ford's established minimums. Specific dollar figures are not published. No
  application fee.\nDuration: 2027-2028 academic year in residence at Stanf
 ord\n\nMore: https://cisac.fsi.stanford.edu/content/cisac-fellowships?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cisac.fsi.stanford.edu/content/cisac-fellowships?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Stanford\, California\, USA (in-residence\; fellows are expected t
 o be fully present and engaged at CISAC)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:generator-residency-winter-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261106T132530Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Generator Residency (Kairos x Constellation\, Winter 2027
 )
DESCRIPTION:A three-month residency for AI safety generalists: builders\, o
 perators and organizers rather than researchers. Residents pitch\, build a
 nd ship their own projects with weekly advice from field leaders\, then ge
 t support landing a full-time AI safety role.\n\nOrganisation: Kairos and 
 Constellation\nLocation: Berkeley\, California\, USA (Constellation office
 ). Core residency is in person\; J-1 visa sponsorship available for most i
 nternational applicants.\nAward: USD 8\,500 per month stipend (some Embedd
 ed track residents employed at a roughly equivalent salary)\, plus travel 
 to and from Berkeley. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 months full-time (1
 8 January to 9 April 2027)\; selected residents can extend in person until
  late May and remotely until early July 2027.\n\nMore: https://generatorre
 sidency.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://generatorresidency.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berkeley\, California\, USA (Constellation office). Core residency
  is in person\; J-1 visa sponsorship available for most international appl
 icants.
END:VEVENT
